{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Cut CI tickets-store transfer cost across both checkout mechanisms. Measured evidence in session_log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4 and the epic comments: recurring actions/checkout full checkout 1.04 GiB / 59 s versus blob:none 68.7 MiB / 14.3 s; Gerrit verify-identity full tickets fetch 6.73 minutes, with local full 1.4 GB / 66.2 s versus blob:none 22 MB / 3.6 s and 83 MB / 8.6 s after worktree materialization. Do not re-derive those historical baselines.\n\n## Scope and mechanisms\nThree recurring workflows use actions/checkout@v7 with fetch-depth: 0, so all-branch tickets history arrives during checkout before the later manual fetch. Add filter: blob:none while preserving fetch depth and existing credentials/ref settings in:\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml\n- .github/workflows/verify-identity.yml\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml\n\nThe subsequent plain git fetch origin +tickets refspec must inherit the named remote partial-clone filter. Config presence is insufficient because Git records partialclonefilter even when a server ignores it. The non-vacuous oracle uses a real Git server with uploadpack.allowFilter=true: configure a named origin blobless, create a previously absent tickets ref with a known blob, fetch it with no explicit filter, require GIT_TRACE_PACKET to contain fetch> filter blob:none, and prove that blob is absent before worktree materialization.\n\nThe Gerrit Verified workflow uses a different mechanism: two direct-URL git fetch commands, so named-remote inheritance cannot reach them. Add --filter=blob:none explicitly to both the depth-1 require-ticket fetch and the full-history verify-identity fetch while preserving their existing depth semantics. The prior measured blobless direct fetch plus worktree add completed successfully and retained the complete commit graph required for era scoping.\n\n## Safety and observability\nNever use filter: tree:0 here: it measured 3.57 GiB across 2,255 promisor packs, 3.4x larger than full. filter and sparse-checkout may coexist; none of the three target all-history checkout steps uses sparse checkout.\n\ngit worktree add uses the unpack-trees -u/check_updates path, which batch-prefetches missing promisor blobs. This differs from the read-tree plus checkout-index path documented in tests/unit/test_snapshot_blobless_747f.py, which can lazy-fetch one blob per RPC. A held-out real-Git E2E must materialize the tickets tree, introduce independent local and remote changes, fetch/merge using the B3 ours driver, retain all expected events, and push successfully.\n\nAdd measured guardrails:\n1. In standalone verify-identity, immediately after actions/checkout parse size-pack from git count-objects -v and fail above 102400 KiB (100 MiB). This is above measured 68.7 MiB but still requires at least 90 percent reduction from 1.04 GiB.\n2. In Gerrit verify-identity, after the filtered fetch and worktree materialization fail if size-pack exceeds 131072 KiB (128 MiB), above the measured 83 MB materialized result but far below 1.4 GB. This makes the current change prove the server honored the direct filter.\n3. In both verify-identity jobs, snapshot exact git count-objects -v output after worktree materialization, run rebar verify-identity, snapshot again, and fail on any difference. Materialization may fetch current-tree blobs; the identity scan must add no loose objects or packs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The three actions/checkout@v7 steps set filter: blob:none and retain fetch-depth: 0 plus existing credentials/ref settings; both gerrit-verify.yaml direct tickets fetches pass --filter=blob:none while retaining depth-1 only on require-ticket and full history on verify-identity. Tier: parsed workflow contract. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -v.\n- [ ] Production CI measurements fail above 102400 KiB immediately after standalone checkout and above 131072 KiB after Gerrit tickets worktree materialization, compared with recorded full baselines of 1.04 GiB and 1.4 GB. A config-only assertion is forbidden. Tier: CI job measurement plus parsed workflow contract. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k size_pack -v.\n- [ ] A plain manual tickets fetch from a named blobless origin inherits the filter: packet trace contains fetch> filter blob:none and a known tickets blob remains absent before worktree materialization. Tier: real temporary Git server/repository. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k inherits_filter -v.\n- [ ] A blobless runner materializes the tickets worktree and reconverges a locally diverged tickets branch against a remote update using the configured ours merge driver; all expected events remain reachable and final push succeeds. Cover both named-origin and explicit direct-fetch setup. Tier: real-Git end to end. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k reconverges -v.\n- [ ] Whole-store verify-identity triggers no promisor fetch: exact git count-objects -v is identical immediately before and after the command in both production identity jobs, and the workflow fails on any difference. Tier: CI job measurement plus real-Git integration. Proving commands: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k no_promisor -v and pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k verify_identity -v.\n\n## Files\n.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml; .github/workflows/verify-identity.yml; .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml; .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml; tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py; tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py.\n\nScope: M. Depends on closed B3 040e-3f0c-ae86-4212 and closed B6 3036-cb14-86b5-44a3.","title":"B1: apply filter: blob:none to every CI tickets-branch fetch path"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785610631548603001,"uuid":"6bc205a4-9e7f-4282-b2d7-eb0d474f748b"}